From 7dc4740d14753a80e56a7f50fb98f7fb15f74a21 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yash Hooda <yash.hooda6@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 01:00:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Add .gitattributes to pin line endings
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A Windows checkout was about to commit CRLF into every file. Harmless for
Python, but CRLF in verify.sh means "bad interpreter" on Linux — a break
that only appears in CI. LF everywhere, except .cmd/.bat which cmd.exe
wants as CRLF.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01YEPpTfqvKcxQrfaydM28UE
---
 .gitattributes | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 .gitattributes

diff --git a/.gitattributes b/.gitattributes
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..f84a09e
--- /dev/null
+++ b/.gitattributes
@@ -0,0 +1,13 @@
+# Normalize line endings. Without this, a Windows checkout commits CRLF into
+# shell scripts, and `verify.sh` then fails on Linux with "bad interpreter" —
+# a failure that only shows up in CI, which is the worst place to find it.
+* text=auto eol=lf
+
+# Batch files are the exception: cmd.exe wants CRLF.
+*.cmd text eol=crlf
+*.bat text eol=crlf
+
+# Never touch these.
+*.db binary
+*.png binary
+*.jpg binary
